      "role": "explain",
      "headline": "Refugees become rebels",
      "body": "The Huns, nomadic horsemen from the Eurasian steppes, were pushing west and driving other peoples before them. In 376 CE Goths fleeing the Huns were allowed to cross the Danube into the empire. Mistreated and exploited by Roman officials, they rebelled."
    },
    {
      "id": "card.ancient_rome.089.c3",
      "type": "text",
      "role": "explain",
      "headline": "The battle",
      "body": "At Adrianople in 378 CE the Goths destroyed a Roman army, and the emperor Valens was killed. Gothic cavalry arriving during the battle played a decisive part in the Roman defeat."
    },
    {
      "id": "card.ancient_rome.089.c4",
      "type": "fact",
      "fact": "Afterwards, the Goths stayed.",
      "context": "Gothic groups settled inside the empire as allies under their own leaders, a new and risky arrangement for Rome."
